{"kind":"final","result":{"schemaVersion":"authorization-inquiry-result/v1","questions":[{"questionId":"q1","behavior":{"disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The document download action calls file_response(pk, request, \"attachment\"). file_response first resolves the requested document/root context, then selects an effective file document, and finally calls serve_file on that selected document. The shown source establishes the file-selection and representation branches, but not the helper implementation that authorizes the authenticated user or the serve_file implementation that opens the returned path."},"branches":[{"id":"download-invalid-or-missing","condition":"The download action or downstream resolution raises FileNotFoundError or Document.DoesNotExist.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The download action converts those exceptions to HTTP 404, so no file is returned.","evidenceIds":["ev-6e0bc39aa0cab4991317"]},{"id":"download-resolution-forbidden","condition":"The request/root-resolution helper returns HttpResponseForbidden.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"file_response explicitly returns an HttpResponseForbidden result from the resolver instead of proceeding to file selection or serve_file. The displayed source does not show which user, object, ownership, or object-grant conditions cause that result.","evidenceIds":["ev-02e44f6c9deb225b1857"]},{"id":"download-authorized-effective-file","condition":"Request/root resolution does not return HttpResponseForbidden and produces a request document and root document.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"file_response calls _get_effective_file_doc(resolved.request_doc, resolved.root_doc, request), then serves that selected file document. The selected resource is therefore determined after request/root resolution, not directly from pk alone. Without the bodies of the resolution and effective-document helpers, it is unresolved whether authorization is checked against the root document, the requested version, the effective file document, or more than one. No owner or object-grant state was supplied, so none is assumed.","evidenceIds":["ev-02e44f6c9deb225b1857"]},{"id":"download-original-representation","condition":"original_requested(request) is true, or the selected file document has no archive version.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"serve_file is called with use_archive equal to not original_requested(request) and file_doc.has_archive_version. Thus an original request selects the original representation; absent an archive version, the archive branch is also false. The source shown does not include serve_file, so the exact path construction and any additional protection are unresolved.","evidenceIds":["ev-02e44f6c9deb225b1857"]},{"id":"download-archive-representation","condition":"original_requested(request) is false and the selected file document has an archive version.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The returned file is requested through serve_file with use_archive=true, selecting the archive representation of the selected effective file document. This changes the representation/file path returned, but the shown source does not establish a separate authorization check for the archive path.","evidenceIds":["ev-02e44f6c9deb225b1857"]},{"id":"download-explicit-version","condition":"The request contains a version selection that is accepted by request/root resolution.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The download path passes the request into request/root resolution and then into _get_effective_file_doc. The available source identifies resolve_requested_version_for_root as a dependency but does not show its body. Therefore selecting another version may change the effective file document and consequently the file returned, but this slice cannot establish whether authorization is re-evaluated for that selected version or remains bound only to the root/requested document.","evidenceIds":["ev-02e44f6c9deb225b1857","ev-6e0bc39aa0c